# The vendored specification files are embedded verbatim into generated Kotlin source, so their
# bytes are part of what ships. Without this, a checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites them to
# CRLF and the embedded constants differ from the specification's own file -- while still parsing as
# JSON and still passing every test, which is the one failure mode vendoring is meant to rule out.
a2ui-core/spec/**       text eol=lf
a2ui-compose/spec/**    text eol=lf
a2ui-gallery/spec/**    text eol=lf

# The vendored Unicode Character Database is the input the `XID_Start` / `XID_Continue` tables are
# derived from, and `a2ui-core/unicode/README.md` records its SHA-256. Without this, a checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites it to CRLF, the recorded digest stops matching a file nobody edited,
# and `generateXidTables` fails on a working tree that is byte-correct in the index.
a2ui-core/unicode/**    text eol=lf
